// REJECTS: Unexpected token '%latest'
//
// `%latest` is CoreLexerGrammar's one keyword and it is not a general-purpose date literal.
// It is a milestoning date parameter, legal only in the argument positions that take one
// (`.all(%latest)`, milestoned property calls). Bound to a variable in a function body it
// is not a value at all.
//
// The whole grammar is a single token, which is exactly why it invites the shortcut: a
// rewrite lexes '%latest' alongside the '%'-prefixed date literals it already handles --
// they share a prefix and a lexer rule shape -- and thereby makes it an expression
// everywhere. Nothing rejects it afterwards, because downstream a date is a date.
###Pure
function fixture::neg::latestValue(): Date[1]
{
   let d = %latest;
   $d;
}
